<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Goriely & Tabor (1998) PRL / Gerbode et al. (2012) Science Kirchhoff elastic rod tendril perversion, G-fiber overwinding & Pass 3 thigmotropic contact coiling (Climbing plant tendrils (Cucumis sativus, Passiflora caerulea, Bryonia dioica, Echinocystis lobata))" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-5> ;
    schema:about "Climbing plant tendrils (Cucumis sativus, Passiflora caerulea, Bryonia dioica, Echinocystis lobata)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Circumnutation or support-search before first touch, a measured tendril-on-wood friction coefficient, compliant or rough or finite-length supports, G-fiber lignification time course, or a validated time-to-wrap (tau_thigmo and v_signal were chosen inside Darwin's 5-60 min window and the model's 4.75 min falls slightly below it)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 3: 61-node inertia-free discrete rod with contact-gated intrinsic curvature pointing toward the support axis, implicit backward-Euler incremental potential (L-BFGS-B), rigid-cylinder penalty contact, penalty self-contact, lagged-normal Coulomb friction on support and self-contact, quasi-static grip test vs mu*sum(N) and exp(mu Theta); no-support, frictionless, friction-sweep, support-radius-sweep and stacked-turns scenarios",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Timoshenko bilayer kappa_0, exact T_c, 161-node L-BFGS-B Kirchhoff perversion solver with zero-link enforcement and negative controls; 10-point pitchfork sweep; soft vs lignified overwinding; 4-species scaling; DoG segmentation of the SHA-256-locked Passiflora caerulea specimen (Pass 2)",
        "reported_in_source: Darwin (1865) Ch. IV: tendrils curve toward a touched side within tens of seconds, complete a wrap around a thin stick within minutes to about an hour, and grasp thin supports more readily than thick ones (qualitative)",
        "reported_in_source: Gerbode et al. (2012): the cucumber tendril's G-fiber ribbon sets the intrinsic curvature; soft tendrils (Gamma < 1) overwind under axial stretch while lignified ones unwind; coil radius and pitch scale across species",
        "reported_in_source: Goriely & Tabor (1998) / McMillen & Goriely (2002): an intrinsically curved Kirchhoff rod with both ends held undergoes a supercritical pitchfork bifurcation below T_c = B kappa_0^2 / (1 + Gamma) into two opposite-handed helices joined by a perversion, with zero net link",
        "reported_in_source: Jaffe & Galston (1968): thigmotropic coiling is a contact-triggered, propagating growth response; Euler (1762): the capstan law exp(mu Theta) for a flexible line on a cylinder",
        "transfer_boundary: Friction uses normal forces lagged one macro step; F_hold / mu*sum(N) = 0.67 is a consistency check of the scheme, not an experiment; N_wrap counts loose loops that enclose but do not touch the support (contact fraction 33 % of nodes)",
        "transfer_boundary: The contact solver is a separate bending-only rod: it has no material-frame twist, so Gamma = C/B plays no role in contact coiling and the perversion (zero-link) physics of section 3 is not coupled to it",
        "transfer_boundary: mu_support, mu_self, kappa_contact, tau_thigmo, v_signal, the 55 deg approach angle and the initial placement touching the support at 25 % of L are provenance-tagged assumptions; the only empirical anchors for Pass 3 are Darwin's qualitative timings and support-size statements" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/s00332-002-0493-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.80.1564>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1095-8339.1865.tb00011.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1223304>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1146/annurev.pp.19.060168.002221>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3732/ajb.0900045> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-10>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-11>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-12>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-13>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-14>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-15>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-8>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-9> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Kirchhoff Elastic Rod Hamiltonian Mechanics, Zero-Link Topological Conservation (ΔLk = 0), Pitchfork Bifurcation, G-Fiber Overwinding & Contact-Gated Thigmotropic Coiling with Coulomb Friction" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 9.17e-01 .

