<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Goriely & Tabor (1998) PRL / Gerbode et al. (2012) Science Kirchhoff elastic rod tendril perversion, G-fiber overwinding & Pass 3 thigmotropic contact coiling — Morphological realism / specimen match: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Unchanged specimen pipeline: the SHA-256-locked CC BY-SA Passiflora caerulea tendril JPG is segmented into backbone, 50 helical turn apices and the perversion zone (`segment_tendril_perversion_specimen` L1144-L1220) and shown in panel E; 4-species coil radius/pitch match (r = 0.9999). Pass 3 adds panels G/H and a 4-panel thigmotropic figure + GIF whose 3D rod wraps a grey cylinder in a visually plausible helix. Deductions: there is no empirical specimen of a tendril wrapped on a support, so the new coiling output is compared only with the no-support control and Darwin's prose (-5); with 33 % of nodes in contact and a mean loop radius above R_s + a, panel G's \"N = 2.9\" includes loose loops that enclose but do not touch the support, so the figure reads tighter than the statistics support (-3); specimen pitch CV 0.298 vs the 0.22 reference is a Pass 2 carry-over that the model does not explain (-2); panel H overlays F_hold(mu) and N_wrap(R_s) on one axes with a secondary top axis, and panel C of the thigmotropic PNG has a legend that partly overlaps the curves (cosmetic)." ;
