<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Zero-Link Topological Conservation & Opposite-Handed Chiral Helix Cancellation Law" ;
    dct:description "Explains why a tethered climbing plant tendril that cannot rotate its ends must coil into two mirror-symmetric helices of opposite chirality (+τ and -τ) joined by a central perversion inversion kink | Variables: τ_h: equilibrium helical Frenet torsion (mm^-1); L_half = L/2: half-tendril arc length (mm); ΔLk: net Călugăreanu-White-Fuller linking number change" ;
    dct:source "Goriely & Tabor (1998) Phys. Rev. Lett. 80:1564-1567; McMillen & Goriely (2002) J. Nonlinear Sci. 12:241-281" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py#L249-L412>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_064_tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature.lean#L27-L36> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def net_chiral_link (tau_plus tau_minus L_half : Int) : Int :=
  tau_plus * L_half + tau_minus * L_half
theorem goriely_zero_link_chiral_cancellation (tau_h L_half : Int) :
    net_chiral_link tau_h (-tau_h) L_half = 0 ∧
    net_chiral_link (-tau_h) tau_h L_half = 0
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "ΔLk = Tw + Wr = 0  ⇒  N_+(+τ_h) + N_-(-τ_h) = 0,  τ(-s) = -τ(s),  τ(0) = 0 at the perversion kink" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/s00332-002-0493-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.80.1564>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1095-8339.1865.tb00011.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1223304>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1146/annurev.pp.19.060168.002221>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3732/ajb.0900045> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Kirchhoff Elastic Rod Hamiltonian Mechanics, Zero-Link Topological Conservation (ΔLk = 0), Pitchfork Bifurcation, G-Fiber Overwinding & Contact-Gated Thigmotropic Coiling with Coulomb Friction" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_064.net_chiral_link" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_064.goriely_zero_link_chiral_cancellation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Goriely & Tabor (1998) Critical Tension Pitchfork Bifurcation & Heteroclinic Perversion Soliton Law" ;
    dct:description "Determines the exact critical tension T_c below which an intrinsically curved rod bifurcates into left- and right-handed helices and governs the spatial width ξ of the central tendril perversion | Variables: T_c: critical buckling tension (mN); B = E I: rod bending stiffness (mN·mm^2); Γ = C/B: twist-to-bend stiffness ratio; κ_0: G-fiber intrinsic curvature (mm^-1); ξ: perversion kink localization length (mm)" ;
    dct:source "Goriely & Tabor (1998) Phys. Rev. Lett. 80:1564-1567 Eq. 11; McMillen & Goriely (2002) J. Nonlinear Sci. 12:241-281 Sec. 3-4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py#L164-L247>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_064_tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature.lean#L54-L62> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def pitchfork_bifurcation_residual (T gamma_plus_1 B kappa0 : Int) : Int :=
  T * gamma_plus_1 - B * (kappa0 * kappa0)
theorem goriely_pitchfork_critical_tension (B kappa0 gamma_plus_1 : Int) :
    pitchfork_bifurcation_residual (B * (kappa0 * kappa0)) 1 B kappa0 = 0 ∧
    pitchfork_bifurcation_residual 0 gamma_plus_1 B 0 = 0
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "T_c = B κ_0^2 / (1 + Γ),  cos θ_helix = 1 - ((1 + Γ)/Γ)(1 - √(T / T_c))  (T ≤ T_c),  θ(s) = θ_helix tanh(s / ξ),  ξ = √(B / (T_c - T))" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/s00332-002-0493-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.80.1564>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1095-8339.1865.tb00011.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1223304>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1146/annurev.pp.19.060168.002221>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3732/ajb.0900045> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Kirchhoff Elastic Rod Hamiltonian Mechanics, Zero-Link Topological Conservation (ΔLk = 0), Pitchfork Bifurcation, G-Fiber Overwinding & Contact-Gated Thigmotropic Coiling with Coulomb Friction" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_064.pitchfork_bifurcation_residual" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_064.goriely_pitchfork_critical_tension" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Gerbode et al. (2012) Soft vs Mature Lignified Tendril Over-Winding Susceptibility Law" ;
    dct:description "Explains the counterintuitive mechanical overwinding of soft young cucumber tendrils upon axial stretching versus monotonic unwinding in mature lignified tendrils | Variables: B: bending stiffness (mN·mm^2); C: twisting stiffness (mN·mm^2); Γ = C/B: twist-to-bend stiffness ratio; ΔN(z/L): change in coil turns under axial extension" ;
    dct:source "Gerbode, Puzey, McCormick & Mahadevan (2012) Science 337(6098):1087-1091 Figs. 3-4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py#L1040-L1089>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_064_tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature.lean#L77-L90> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def gerbode_overwinding_susceptibility (B C : Int) : Int :=
  B - C
theorem gerbode_soft_vs_lignified_overwinding (B dC : Int) :
    gerbode_overwinding_susceptibility B B = 0 ∧
    (∀ k : Nat, gerbode_overwinding_susceptibility (B + Int.ofNat (k + 1)) B = Int.ofNat (k + 1)) ∧
    gerbode_overwinding_susceptibility B (B + dC) = -dC
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "S_overwind = B - C = B(1 - Γ);  Γ = C/B < 1 (young soft G-fiber ribbon) ⇒ dN/dz > 0 (initial axial stretching overwinds coil);  Γ > 1 (old lignified tendril) ⇒ dN/dz < 0 (monotonic unwinding)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/s00332-002-0493-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.80.1564>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1095-8339.1865.tb00011.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1223304>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1146/annurev.pp.19.060168.002221>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3732/ajb.0900045> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Kirchhoff Elastic Rod Hamiltonian Mechanics, Zero-Link Topological Conservation (ΔLk = 0), Pitchfork Bifurcation, G-Fiber Overwinding & Contact-Gated Thigmotropic Coiling with Coulomb Friction" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_064.gerbode_overwinding_susceptibility" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_064.gerbode_soft_vs_lignified_overwinding" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Contact-Gated Thigmotropic Intrinsic Curvature Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Drives the Pass 3 dynamic contact-coiling solver: a straight tendril acquires intrinsic curvature toward the support only where and after it is touched, so coiling is contact-induced and the no-support control stays straight (Darwin 1865 positive thigmotropism; Jaffe & Galston 1968) | Variables: κ_contact: saturating thigmotropic curvature of the touched flank (mm^-1, assumption 1.0); τ_thigmo: curvature rise time after signal arrival (min, assumption 5); v_signal: touch-signal propagation speed along the rod (mm/min, assumption 5); t_arrive_i: signal arrival time at node i" ;
    dct:source "Darwin (1865) J. Linn. Soc. Bot. 9:1-118 Ch. IV; Jaffe & Galston (1968) Annu. Rev. Plant Physiol. 19:417-434" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py#L596-L909>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_064_tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature.lean#L110-L122> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def gated_curvature (touched : Bool) (kappa_contact r : Nat) : Nat :=
  if touched then kappa_contact * r else 0
theorem thigmotropic_contact_gating (kappa_contact r d : Nat) (h : r ≤ d) :
    gated_curvature false kappa_contact r = 0 ∧
    gated_curvature true kappa_contact d = kappa_contact * d ∧
    gated_curvature true kappa_contact r ≤ kappa_contact * d
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "κ0_i(t) = κ_contact · [t ≥ t_arrive_i] · (1 − exp(−(t − t_arrive_i)/τ_thigmo)),  t_arrive_i = min_j (t_touch_j + |s_i − s_j| / v_signal);  no touch ⇒ κ0 ≡ 0 ⇒ no coiling;  0 ≤ κ0_i ≤ κ_contact" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/s00332-002-0493-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.80.1564>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1095-8339.1865.tb00011.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1223304>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1146/annurev.pp.19.060168.002221>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3732/ajb.0900045> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Kirchhoff Elastic Rod Hamiltonian Mechanics, Zero-Link Topological Conservation (ΔLk = 0), Pitchfork Bifurcation, G-Fiber Overwinding & Contact-Gated Thigmotropic Coiling with Coulomb Friction" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_064.gated_curvature" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_064.thigmotropic_contact_gating" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Amontons-Coulomb Friction Grip Capacity of the Wrapped Tendril (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Explains why a coiled tendril holds the plant on its support only when friction and squeeze are both present; measured in the Pass 3 quasi-static load-ramp grip test and friction sweep (F_hold/μΣN ≈ 0.67 at default parameters) | Variables: μ: tendril-on-support Coulomb friction coefficient (assumption 0.6, swept 0-0.9); N_i: penalty normal force at contacting node i (mN); F_hold: axial load at which the wrapped segment slips 0.5 mm (mN); Θ_wrap: total wrap angle (rad)" ;
    dct:source "Amontons (1699) / Coulomb (1785) friction law; Euler (1762) Mém. Acad. Roy. Sci. Berlin 18:265-278 (capstan law); Darwin (1865) Ch. IV" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py#L911-L977>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_064_tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature.lean#L135-L146> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def coulomb_capacity (mu N : Nat) : Nat :=
  mu * N
theorem coulomb_grip_capacity (mu1 mu2 N : Nat) (h : mu1 ≤ mu2) :
    coulomb_capacity 0 N = 0 ∧
    coulomb_capacity mu1 0 = 0 ∧
    coulomb_capacity mu1 N ≤ coulomb_capacity mu2 N
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "F_hold ≤ μ Σ_i N_i  (incremental-potential Coulomb friction with lagged normal forces);  μ = 0 ⇒ F_hold = 0 (frictionless control slips);  F_hold(μ) non-decreasing;  capstan reference gain T_hold/T_load = exp(μ Θ_wrap) (Euler 1762)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/s00332-002-0493-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.80.1564>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1095-8339.1865.tb00011.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1223304>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1146/annurev.pp.19.060168.002221>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3732/ajb.0900045> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Kirchhoff Elastic Rod Hamiltonian Mechanics, Zero-Link Topological Conservation (ΔLk = 0), Pitchfork Bifurcation, G-Fiber Overwinding & Contact-Gated Thigmotropic Coiling with Coulomb Friction" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_064.coulomb_capacity" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_064.coulomb_grip_capacity" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

