<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Contact-Gated Thigmotropic Intrinsic Curvature Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Drives the Pass 3 dynamic contact-coiling solver: a straight tendril acquires intrinsic curvature toward the support only where and after it is touched, so coiling is contact-induced and the no-support control stays straight (Darwin 1865 positive thigmotropism; Jaffe & Galston 1968) | Variables: κ_contact: saturating thigmotropic curvature of the touched flank (mm^-1, assumption 1.0); τ_thigmo: curvature rise time after signal arrival (min, assumption 5); v_signal: touch-signal propagation speed along the rod (mm/min, assumption 5); t_arrive_i: signal arrival time at node i" ;
    dct:source "Darwin (1865) J. Linn. Soc. Bot. 9:1-118 Ch. IV; Jaffe & Galston (1968) Annu. Rev. Plant Physiol. 19:417-434" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py#L596-L909>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_064_tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature.lean#L110-L122> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def gated_curvature (touched : Bool) (kappa_contact r : Nat) : Nat :=
  if touched then kappa_contact * r else 0
theorem thigmotropic_contact_gating (kappa_contact r d : Nat) (h : r ≤ d) :
    gated_curvature false kappa_contact r = 0 ∧
    gated_curvature true kappa_contact d = kappa_contact * d ∧
    gated_curvature true kappa_contact r ≤ kappa_contact * d
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "κ0_i(t) = κ_contact · [t ≥ t_arrive_i] · (1 − exp(−(t − t_arrive_i)/τ_thigmo)),  t_arrive_i = min_j (t_touch_j + |s_i − s_j| / v_signal);  no touch ⇒ κ0 ≡ 0 ⇒ no coiling;  0 ≤ κ0_i ≤ κ_contact" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/s00332-002-0493-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.80.1564>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1095-8339.1865.tb00011.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1223304>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1146/annurev.pp.19.060168.002221>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3732/ajb.0900045> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Kirchhoff Elastic Rod Hamiltonian Mechanics, Zero-Link Topological Conservation (ΔLk = 0), Pitchfork Bifurcation, G-Fiber Overwinding & Contact-Gated Thigmotropic Coiling with Coulomb Friction" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_064.gated_curvature" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_064.thigmotropic_contact_gating" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Amontons-Coulomb Friction Grip Capacity of the Wrapped Tendril (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Explains why a coiled tendril holds the plant on its support only when friction and squeeze are both present; measured in the Pass 3 quasi-static load-ramp grip test and friction sweep (F_hold/μΣN ≈ 0.67 at default parameters) | Variables: μ: tendril-on-support Coulomb friction coefficient (assumption 0.6, swept 0-0.9); N_i: penalty normal force at contacting node i (mN); F_hold: axial load at which the wrapped segment slips 0.5 mm (mN); Θ_wrap: total wrap angle (rad)" ;
    dct:source "Amontons (1699) / Coulomb (1785) friction law; Euler (1762) Mém. Acad. Roy. Sci. Berlin 18:265-278 (capstan law); Darwin (1865) Ch. IV" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py#L911-L977>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_064_tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature.lean#L135-L146> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def coulomb_capacity (mu N : Nat) : Nat :=
  mu * N
theorem coulomb_grip_capacity (mu1 mu2 N : Nat) (h : mu1 ≤ mu2) :
    coulomb_capacity 0 N = 0 ∧
    coulomb_capacity mu1 0 = 0 ∧
    coulomb_capacity mu1 N ≤ coulomb_capacity mu2 N
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "F_hold ≤ μ Σ_i N_i  (incremental-potential Coulomb friction with lagged normal forces);  μ = 0 ⇒ F_hold = 0 (frictionless control slips);  F_hold(μ) non-decreasing;  capstan reference gain T_hold/T_load = exp(μ Θ_wrap) (Euler 1762)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/s00332-002-0493-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.80.1564>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1095-8339.1865.tb00011.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1223304>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1146/annurev.pp.19.060168.002221>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3732/ajb.0900045> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Kirchhoff Elastic Rod Hamiltonian Mechanics, Zero-Link Topological Conservation (ΔLk = 0), Pitchfork Bifurcation, G-Fiber Overwinding & Contact-Gated Thigmotropic Coiling with Coulomb Friction" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_064.coulomb_capacity" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_064.coulomb_grip_capacity" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

